.IX Title "EVP_KDF-SRTPKDF 7ossl"
.TH EVP_KDF-SRTPKDF 7ossl "2026-04-14" "4.0.0" "OpenSSL"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
EVP_KDF\-SRTPKDF \- The SRTP EVP_KDF implementation
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Support for computing the \fB\s-1SRTP\s0\fR \s-1KDF\s0 through the \fB\s-1EVP_KDF\s0\fR \s-1API.\s0
.PP
The \s-1EVP_KDF\-SRTP\s0 algorithm implements the \s-1SRTP\s0 key derivation function.
\&\s-1SRTP\s0 follows the specification in \s-1RFC 3711\s0 Section 4.3.3, where various
cryptographic keys (encryption, authentication, and salt keys) are derived
from a master key and master salt using \s-1AES\s0 encryption with specific labels.
.PP
The output keys are used for \s-1SRTP\s0 and \s-1SRTCP\s0 packet protection.
.SS "Identity"
.IX Subsection "Identity"
\&\*(L"\s-1SRTP\*(R"\s0 is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
\&\fIEVP_KDF_fetch()\fR function.
.SS "Supported parameters"
.IX Subsection "Supported parameters"
The supported parameters are:
.ie n .IP """properties"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES\s0\fR) <\s-1UTF8\s0 string>" 4
.el .IP "``properties'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES\s0\fR) <\s-1UTF8\s0 string>" 4
.IX Item "properties (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES) <UTF8 string>"
.PD 0
.ie n .IP """cipher"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER\s0\fR) <\s-1UTF8\s0 string>" 4
.el .IP "``cipher'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER\s0\fR) <\s-1UTF8\s0 string>" 4
.IX Item "cipher (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER) <UTF8 string>"
.PD
This parameter sets the cipher to be used for the key derivation.
It must be set to one of \*(L"\s-1AES\-128\-CTR\*(R", \*(L"AES\-192\-CTR\*(R"\s0 or \*(L"\s-1AES\-256\-CTR\*(R".\s0
.ie n .IP """key"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.el .IP "``key'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item "key (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY) <octet string>"
This parameter sets the master key value. This must be 16 bytes for \s-1AES\-128,
24\s0 bytes for \s-1AES\-192\s0 or 32 bytes for \s-1AES\-256.\s0
.ie n .IP """salt"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.el .IP "``salt'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item "salt (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT) <octet string>"
This parameter sets the master salt value. The must be at least 14 bytes.
Note that larger salts are truncated.
.ie n .IP """kdr"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_KDR\s0\fR) <unsigned integer>" 4
.el .IP "``kdr'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_KDR\s0\fR) <unsigned integer>" 4
.IX Item "kdr (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_KDR) <unsigned integer>"
This parameter sets the key derivation rate (\s-1KDR\s0). The \s-1KDR\s0 controls
how often keys are rederived. If not set or set to zero, no key
rederivation is performed. The \s-1KDR\s0 value is power of 2 in the range 2^0 to 2^24.
.ie n .IP """index"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_INDEX\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.el .IP "``index'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_INDEX\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item "index (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_INDEX) <octet string>"
This parameter sets the index value used in key derivation. The length must be
at least 6 bytes for \s-1RTP\s0 packets, or at least 4 bytes for \s-1RTCP\s0 packets.
Note that larger index values are truncated.
If it is not set, or it has zero length, no key rederivation is performed.
.ie n .IP """label"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_LABEL\s0\fR) <unsigned integer>" 4
.el .IP "``label'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_LABEL\s0\fR) <unsigned integer>" 4
.IX Item "label (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_LABEL) <unsigned integer>"
This parameter sets the label that identifies the type of key to derive.
Valid values are:
.RS 4
.IP "0 \- \s-1SRTP\s0 encryption key" 4
.IX Item "0 - SRTP encryption key"
.PD 0
.IP "1 \- \s-1SRTP\s0 authentication key" 4
.IX Item "1 - SRTP authentication key"
.IP "2 \- \s-1SRTP\s0 salt key" 4
.IX Item "2 - SRTP salt key"
.IP "3 \- \s-1SRTCP\s0 encryption key" 4
.IX Item "3 - SRTCP encryption key"
.IP "4 \- \s-1SRTCP\s0 authentication key" 4
.IX Item "4 - SRTCP authentication key"
.IP "5 \- \s-1SRTCP\s0 salt key" 4
.IX Item "5 - SRTCP salt key"
.IP "6 \- \s-1SRTP\s0 encryption key (alternative)" 4
.IX Item "6 - SRTP encryption key (alternative)"
.IP "7 \- \s-1SRTP\s0 salt key (alternative)" 4
.IX Item "7 - SRTP salt key (alternative)"
.RE
.RS 4
.RE
.PD
.SH "NOTES"
.IX Header "NOTES"
A context for \s-1SRTP\s0 can be obtained by calling:
.PP
.Vb 2
\& EVP_KDF *kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "SRTP", NULL);
\& EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
.Ve
.PP
The output length of the \s-1SRTP KDF\s0 derive operation is determined by the label:
.IP "Labels 0, 3, 6: Output length equals the cipher key length" 4
.IX Item "Labels 0, 3, 6: Output length equals the cipher key length"
.PD 0
.IP "Labels 1, 4: Output length is 20 bytes (160 bits)" 4
.IX Item "Labels 1, 4: Output length is 20 bytes (160 bits)"
.IP "Labels 2, 5, 7: Output length is 14 bytes (112 bits)" 4
.IX Item "Labels 2, 5, 7: Output length is 14 bytes (112 bits)"
.PD
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
This example derives an \s-1SRTP\s0 encryption key (label 0) using \s-1AES\-128\-CTR\s0
with a 16\-byte master key and 14\-byte master salt:
.PP
.Vb 7
\& EVP_KDF *kdf;
\& EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx;
\& unsigned char out[16];
\& unsigned char master_key[16] = { /* master key bytes */ };
\& unsigned char master_salt[14] = { /* master salt bytes */ };
\& uint32_t label = 0;
\& OSSL_PARAM params[5], *p = params;
\&
\& kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "SRTP", NULL);
\& kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
\& EVP_KDF_free(kdf);
\&
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER,
\&                                         "AES\-128\-CTR", 0);
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY,
\&                                          master_key, sizeof(master_key));
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT,
\&                                          master_salt, sizeof(master_salt));
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_uint32(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_LABEL, &label);
\& *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
\&
\& if (EVP_KDF_derive(kctx, out, sizeof(out), params) <= 0) {
\&     error("EVP_KDF_derive");
\& }
\&
\& EVP_KDF_CTX_free(kctx);
.Ve
.PP
This example derives an \s-1SRTP\s0 authentication key (label 1) with key derivation
rate and index:
.PP
.Vb 9
\& EVP_KDF *kdf;
\& EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx;
\& unsigned char out[20];
\& unsigned char master_key[16] = { /* master key bytes */ };
\& unsigned char master_salt[14] = { /* master salt bytes */ };
\& uint32_t kdr = 0x1000; /* KDR */
\& unsigned char index[6] = { 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x01 }; /* index */
\& uint32_t label = 1;
\& OSSL_PARAM params[7], *p = params;
\&
\& kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "SRTP", NULL);
\& kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
\& EVP_KDF_free(kdf);
\&
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER,
\&                                         "AES\-128\-CTR", 0);
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY,
\&                                          master_key, sizeof(master_key));
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT,
\&                                          master_salt, sizeof(master_salt));
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_uint32(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_KDR, &kdr);
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_INDEX,
\&                                          index, sizeof(index));
\& *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_uint32(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SRTPKDF_LABEL, &label);
\& *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
\&
\& if (EVP_KDF_derive(kctx, out, sizeof(out), params) <= 0) {
\&     error("EVP_KDF_derive");
\& }
\&
\& EVP_KDF_CTX_free(kctx);
.Ve
.SH "CONFORMING TO"
.IX Header "CONFORMING TO"
\&\s-1RFC 3711\s0 Section 4.3.3 (\s-1SRTP\s0 Key Derivation)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\s-1\fIEVP_KDF\s0\fR\|(3),
\&\fIEVP_KDF_CTX_new\fR\|(3),
\&\fIEVP_KDF_CTX_free\fR\|(3),
\&\fIEVP_KDF_CTX_set_params\fR\|(3),
\&\fIEVP_KDF_derive\fR\|(3),
\&\*(L"\s-1PARAMETERS\*(R"\s0 in \s-1\fIEVP_KDF\s0\fR\|(3)
.SH "HISTORY"
.IX Header "HISTORY"
The \s-1SRTPKDF\s0 was added in OpenSSL 4.0.0.
